  "changes": [
    [
      "Opaque pearl ribbons over a glowing mosaic core instead of the sketch's clear glass",
      "R337 (Ryan, Nov 19): the Glasswright finish is opaque reflective pearl with glowing stained-glass panels; nothing see-through."
    ],
    [
      "Each hangar lens is a shallow well in the mosaic skin with a pearl lip and a stored-light floor, three Starlings parked on it",
      "carrier.md: lenses grown into the skin, not cut openings or pods; Starlings visible; opaque, so the floor is light, not a window."
    ],
    [
      "The sketch's extra stern and flank lens rings are left out; one large stern optic carries the bloom",
      "Weapon match (R241): only data.js weapons show as lenses (one pulsar F, one turret T); the rings read as more guns."
    ],
    [
      "Ribbons slide above and below each hangar lens",
      "So the lens stays clear and reads as grown into the skin."
    ]
  ],
